      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "An expensive ergonomic chair purchased specifically for your studio work likely qualifies as a legitimate business expense and deduction, but it's important first to establish if your home office setup is regular and exclusive to your business use. If you are self-employed and maintaining a home office for client work, QuickBooks QuickBooks can categorize this under Furniture or Equipment in your fixed assets section, which then allows you to claim either a full deduction immediately (if under the expense threshold) or spread the cost over 7 years using depreciation, depending on your company's accounting policy and local tax laws. Before finalizing this, verify the purchase was made with a business credit card or business funds to ensure proper documentation for your tax return.",
