      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While occasional personal use is often overlooked by tax authorities, maintaining strict documentation that the chair was primarily for business is always the safest approach to avoid potential audit issues. Regarding the unaccounted petty cash and fees, inconsistent tracking is common for freelancers starting out, but it could also indicate transaction recording errors or the use of unlinked credit cards that need immediate reconciliation. You should prioritize verifying your source for that leftover cash and writing off genuine vendor fees to prevent tax discrepancies. Addressing these gaps will give you much clearer confidence about your actual financial standing and prevent complications when filing your annual return.",
